{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/157705-lucifuge-turning-them-into-a-major-template","id":157705,"title":"Lucifuge, turning them into a Major Template?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-03T03:52:33-07:00","id":157705,"title":"Lucifuge, turning them into a Major Template?","content":"I've had this bug of an idea of turning the Lucifuge into a 5 dot power stat mini-Major template, ala the Purified, with it's own splat abilities, power stat, juice, et al. However, I am completely shite with mechanics, and not sure where to start. The first order is, well, naming them, then detailing what they do. One of the major problems is how to turn Castigation into a good splat ability. Being hard capped to only 5 abilities isn't very useful. It'd also be good to use three stats into their roll instead of just the current 2, so either add Castigation to the roll, or their power stat.<br /> <br /> Anyways, does this idea interest anyone else?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T06:08:05-07:00","id":157758,"title":"","content":"I've also thought about doing something similar","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T09:43:50-07:00","id":157968,"title":"","content":"Actually I had a thought about doing an &quot;experiment&quot; in which every conspiracy is treated as a separate major template- but I was too lazy :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T10:04:40-07:00","id":157983,"title":"","content":"I'de sugest looking at the book Inferno. It details Demons from a realm of hellish Sin and Vice, which the Lucifuge are the decendants of. In that book, theres a type of semi-major template called The Possessed, which are mortals who have become possessed by these demons of sin and vice to a bigger or lesser degree. Kinda like a Sin-Eater, but with an evil demonic influence, instead of a Geist. They have their own selection of interesting and diverse powers related to demonic sin and the manifestation of infernal power.<br /> Wouldn't be too hard to adapt the Lucifuge to be something along these lines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T11:44:49-07:00","id":158080,"title":"","content":"Yeah, just using The Possessed without the clash between the human and the demon is probably a great solution for the Lucifuge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T12:59:04-07:00","id":158157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/157705-lucifuge-turning-them-into-a-major-template?p=158080#post158080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, just using The Possessed without the clash between the human and the demon is probably a great solution for the Lucifuge.</div> </div> </div> </div>With nWoD 1.0, it works perfect. However if you're using the GMC, you're gonna have problems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T13:05:51-07:00","id":158179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/157705-lucifuge-turning-them-into-a-major-template?p=158157#post158157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> With nWoD 1.0, it works perfect. However if you're using the GMC, you're gonna have problems.</div> </div> </div> </div>I should have specified, yes I'd use GMC. As for using the Possessed? I'm not quite happy with how Investments work. I have Inferno, but find the splat to be not what I'm looking for. I'd like it to have a Fuel and Power Stat, along with keeping Castigation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T14:50:12-07:00","id":158313,"title":"","content":"Well, figuring out and tagging on a Fuel stat and power stat to The Possessed shouldn't be too difficult. You could just use the Infernal Will that The Possessed allready have, as an full-on Fuel stat. You could use something that describes their respective infernal rank as their power stat, and call it something like Dominion or Pandemonium. Morality actually seems like a pretty good stat to keep in this case, even as everyone else has Integraty.<br /> As for Castigations, just have two seperate groups of Supernatural Abillities. Like Sin-Eaters have both Manifestations and Ceremonies. These Super-Lucifuge could have Vestments as major Supernatural Powers, seeing as their generally more powerful than Castigations, and kinda link together under a common theme.<br /> The Castigations on the other hand, could be their Ceremonies, being stand-alone powers, without a really grand unifying theme other than their Infernal nature. You could even keep the divide that exists now, in that Vestments have the possibillity of causing Burnout, while Castigations generally have some minor negative downside to them, regardless of how often you use them.<br /> That could possibly make it, so that one group isn't inherently better than the other, just different. Vestments are more powerful, but can be used rarely. Castigations are hardly as powerful as Vestments, but can be used often without fear of dying to Burnout.<br /> Thats my 5 cents anyway. Could actually make for en interesting splat, in my opinion.<br /> <br /> What about The Possessed is it you dont like?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T16:46:24-07:00","id":158406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krobeles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/157705-lucifuge-turning-them-into-a-major-template?p=158313#post158313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, figuring out and tagging on a Fuel stat and power stat to The Possessed shouldn't be too difficult. You could just use the Infernal Will that The Possessed allready have, as an full-on Fuel stat. You could use something that describes their respective infernal rank as their power stat, and call it something like Dominion or Pandemonium. Morality actually seems like a pretty good stat to keep in this case, even as everyone else has Integraty.<br /> As for Castigations, just have two seperate groups of Supernatural Abillities. Like Sin-Eaters have both Manifestations and Ceremonies. These Super-Lucifuge could have Vestments as major Supernatural Powers, seeing as their generally more powerful than Castigations, and kinda link together under a common theme.<br /> The Castigations on the other hand, could be their Ceremonies, being stand-alone powers, without a really grand unifying theme other than their Infernal nature. You could even keep the divide that exists now, in that Vestments have the possibillity of causing Burnout, while Castigations generally have some minor negative downside to them, regardless of how often you use them.<br /> That could possibly make it, so that one group isn't inherently better than the other, just different. Vestments are more powerful, but can be used rarely. Castigations are hardly as powerful as Vestments, but can be used often without fear of dying to Burnout.<br /> Thats my 5 cents anyway. Could actually make for en interesting splat, in my opinion.<br /> <br /> What about The Possessed is it you dont like?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You make a compelling case, I admit. Though, I don't like Demonic Will as a fuel or power stat. I think it works for the Possessed, but not so much for the Supifuge, I think it misses out on some of the game play you get with having ways to refuel your stat, and the flavor a good Power Stat can give. I think Vestments make a good greater power, but I wouldn't quite compare Castigation to Sorcery of any stripe, some of it is a bit like it, others not so much. However, what concerns me is that there are some overlap between the two. Regardless, I'm going to go back and read the Possessed see if there is anything to use from it.<br /> <br /> x-splat: Sins (Wrath, Sloth, ect)<br /> Power Stat: No idea yet. &gt;&lt;<br /> Fuel Stat: Maleficence<br /> Gained by wanton acts of destruction, killing evil spirit creatures (Gain maleficence equal to Rank?), blood sacrifice, 1 per day upon waking from Infernal heritage. <br /> Morality stat: Either Integrity or Corruption (A reverse Integrity, I'd say. Any ideas on Questions?)<br /> <br /> Of course, I'd say they get 10 merit dots.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T18:49:16-07:00","id":158519,"title":"","content":"Use Corruption as the fuel stat. Refill by causing others to sin against their own current morality score, same as a demon would enact its Malepraxis. The Lucifuge are descendents of the royal bloodlines of Hell, so any sin they can get a mortal to commit works, but they gain more if the sin is in alignment with the Lucifuge's own vice. This lets you have the conflict between the Hunter's need to fuel his powers to wield against the forces of darkness, and becoming a worse malignance himself. <br /> <br /> Morality stat seems like it'd be about the degree you've accepted your demonic nature versus how much you fight against those impulses. Thus a good versus evil type scale, with reaching zero leading to shedding the part of you that was once human entirely and becoming a proper demon. <br /> <br /> Castigation, as I understand it, is a mechanism of drawing on the Infernal Power without being corrupted by it. Ritual means to bring the power forth in a controlled fashion, whereas other Children of the Seventh Generation just have it bloom forth in whatever form the Pit decides is appropriate to <b>its</b> plans. I'd use Castigation dots as a limiter for what Vestments you can safely manefest. You can learn higher power Vestments, but if you invoke them, you risk losing control to your inborn demonic instincts. I'm visualizing that as a sort of quasi-frenzy where you do as much damage, physically, emotionally, etc as you can to whatever targets are most succeptible for the duration. This may mean beating a fallen enemy to death, or saying cruel things to your loved ones that would hurt them far more than seeing you flip out and come at them with a knife. <br /> <br /> No idea what to call the power stat, but I'm thinking something that invokes a blooming flower or a chrysalis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1764-cesario","name":"Cesario","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T19:57:29-07:00","id":158589,"title":"","content":"How about this;<br /> <br /> Power Stat: Infernal Power<br /> Fuel Stat: Corruption (Though I like Maleficence)<br /> Morality: Well... I like Corruption as one, but how about we re-purpose Torment?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T10:06:39-07:00","id":159170,"title":"","content":"I was also thinking about reworking the Lucifuge, but not with a power stat and fuel. The base Idea is to rework Castigation as a temptation-to-power kind of thing. Additionally, although Castigations are described as &quot;Rituals&quot;, most of them seem to work more like powers which are just activated, similar to Disciplines.<br /> <br /> Systems: Every time a Lucifuge looses a dot of Integrity (starting with integrity 7 falling to 6), he or she automatically gains a Castigation tied to the lost dot. However, the Lucifuge cannot control it directly, it activates automatically whenever he or she gets a possibility to help fulfill his or her vice with it. If the Lucifuge rises his or her integrity, he or she gains control over the power as long as she has the corresponding dot of integrity.<br /> <br /> Essentially, the Lucifuge has the choice between a lot of power and a low Integrity, or just some powers and a normal Integrity. The individuals who manage to lower their integrity to get many powers and rise it again to control all of them are to be admired (or feared?) indeed. The Lucifure (as organization) will hunt down those who fall too much to the temptation of power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1125-gflash","name":"gflash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1125_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T16:20:34-07:00","id":159435,"title":"","content":"I have a sneaking suspicion that we'll get something like this in Heirs to Hell (for Demon the Descent.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-05T05:28:19-07:00","id":159913,"title":"","content":"One idea I had for enhancing the capacities of the hunters was to borrow the mana rules from Mirrors, with how to replenish their mojo being dependent on which conspiracy one belongs to.<br /> <br /> Lucifuge, since it would embody their authority over hell, it would probably refill by acting in a proud fashion, as if their powers had the vice of Pride. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}